/*! \page Build
Building RL Inference Library
------------------------------

Supported CI toolchains:
------------------------
- Ubuntu 22.04, Windows Server 2022 (Visual Studio 2022), and macOS 15 Intel.
- A C++14 compiler, CMake 3.31.6, Ninja 1.12.1, and Git.
- Windows: install the Visual Studio C++ build tools and a Windows SDK, then
  run commands from an x64 Developer Command Prompt.
- Managed bindings and tests: .NET 10 SDK. Windows also needs the `dotnet-t4`
  tool (`dotnet tool install --global dotnet-t4`).

Initialize dependencies:
-------------------------
On Windows, enable long paths before checking out the recursive submodules:

\verbatim
git config --global core.longpaths true
git submodule update --init --recursive
ext_libs\vcpkg\bootstrap-vcpkg.bat -disableMetrics
\endverbatim

On Linux and macOS:

\verbatim
git submodule update --init --recursive
./ext_libs/vcpkg/bootstrap-vcpkg.sh -disableMetrics
\endverbatim

Use the checked-in vcpkg revision and manifest rather than the runner's global
vcpkg installation. The manifest pins dependency versions, including cpprestsdk.
The shared CI setup is in `.github/actions/setup-build/action.yml`; its binary
cache includes the vcpkg revision, manifest, platform, and build configuration.

Build and test:
---------------
\verbatim
cmake --preset vcpkg-debug
cmake --build --preset vcpkg-debug
ctest --preset vcpkg-debug
\endverbatim

Replace `vcpkg-debug` with `vcpkg-release` for an optimized build. To enable the
standalone parser in the same build, add `-DRL_BUILD_EXTERNAL_PARSER=ON` to
the configure command. To enable managed bindings, add
`-Drlclientlib_BUILD_DOTNET=ON`.

Important targets include `rlclientlib` (API), `rltest` (native tests),
`binary_parser_unit_tests` (when the parser is enabled), and `rl_client`
(when `-DRL_BUILD_PYTHON=ON` is set).

Python wheels:
---------------
CI builds and installs CPython 3.11-3.14 wheels in a digest-pinned
manylinux_2_28 x86-64 image. Inside that image, after initializing dependencies:

\verbatim
PYTHON=/opt/python/cp311-cp311/bin/python bash ./.scripts/linux/build-python-wheel.sh
\endverbatim

The script writes repaired wheels to `audit_output`. The wheel test jobs install
each wheel into a separate Python container and run the binding unit tests.
Python 3.6-3.9 are end-of-life and are no longer in the CI support matrix.
    + reinforcement_learning/examples/rl_sim_cpp
*/
